#section(title: "Graph authoring and serial control", lead: "Typed state and declared routes define one control decision per activation.", body: [
A #term("term-graph") records each #term("term-activation"), its authorized #term("term-attempt") and accepted #term("term-receipt").

#subsection(title: "Definition and node binding")[
#answers(title: "Graph definition", responsibility: [Bind independently typed operations into one application state protocol with native final output.], interface: [definition.new(identity, entry, nodes, state codec, answer codec), node(select, accept, destinations), with_max_activations and build. Commands are Continue(state, NodeId) or Finish(state, answer).], interactions: [Select projects current state to native input; accept combines state and typed output. The bound node erases private input/output types behind encoded boundary callbacks.], invariants: [Construction rejects invalid ids, duplicate nodes, missing entry, unknown destinations and every operation configuration problem. Cycles are allowed but count activations; default maximum is 100.], failure: [Select/accept errors and destination outside the declared set refuse transition. Initial state, selected input, next state and answer must encode and decode. Purity is an author obligation checked only indirectly by bounded callback execution.])

