#section(title: "External jobs and cancellation ownership", lead: "Submission, observation and cancellation evidence retain different meanings.", body: [
An external #term("term-job") remains independent of the local observation lifetime.

#subsection(title: "Receipt and observation")[
#answers(title: "External job port", responsibility: [Observe a previously submitted external job to a checked business outcome.], interface: [graph/job defines a retained receipt/output contract and typed progress; operation.await_job is read-only, own_job also binds a stop request and failure classifier. Submission is a separate fenced activity.], interactions: [Application adapter chooses Saga, Grind or another service and stable logical submission key. Manual poll_job is default; a retained positive poll interval uses leased discovery.], invariants: [Submission acknowledgement proves accepted submission, never business completion. Retrying a logical submission requires downstream idempotency or authoritative lookup. A receipt grants only its declared ownership.], failure: [Lost submission receipt without lookup is uncertain. Read failure keeps waiting; a later completed outcome commits once and no further remote read is needed for that result.])

]
#subsection(title: "Owned stop progress")[

#md-table(3, ([*Progress*], [*Evidence*], [*Allowed follow-up*], [Queued], [Stop intent and authority committed; request not started], [Recovery may execute after its fence.], [Started], [Stop body admitted and may have acted], [Interrupted request is uncertain, never automatically repeated.], [Accepted], [Service accepted the stop request], [Observe terminal outcome; this does not prove cancellation.], [Refused / uncertain], [Definite refusal / unknown stop outcome], [Keep original receipt and inspect authority; no success route after local stop.], [Remote stopped / completed / failed], [Authoritative terminal evidence], [Retain actual disposition and end cleanup without business acceptance.]))
#answers(title: "Owned job cleanup", responsibility: [Preserve a stop obligation that can outlive local cancellation or expiration.], interface: [OwnedJob policy target admits cancellation ownership; StopReason is caller cancellation or retained deadline expiration.], interactions: [Commit stop cause before requests. Request callback passes its own confirmed fence and reuses the existing work grant even after ancestral business admission closes.], invariants: [Later local stop does not replace first committed cause or erase uncertainty. A completed remote artifact is retained if completion wins; stop acknowledgement never overwrites it.], failure: [Unresolved cleanup retains family. Manual or scheduled authoritative observation resolves accepted/refused/uncertain stop state. No routing callback runs after cancellation/expiration.])

]
#subsection(title: "Scheduled observation")[
#answers(title: "Polling schedule", responsibility: [Rediscover due observation without permanent tasks or VM timer authority.], interface: [Observer with retained interval; discovery Poll trigger may also carry an absolute deadline. The first ready claim is immediately due.], interactions: [Backend claims free eligible runs atomically with lease, wait key, dependency revision and claim time. Concurrent scanners claim disjoint work. Recovery revalidates saved root and contracts.], invariants: [Next claim is at least the interval after successful prior claim. Manual observation does not move this automatic schedule. Metadata refresh preserves same-key schedule time.], failure: [Scan interval, batches, unavailable callbacks and lease expiry can delay observation; no completion-latency SLA follows. Failed claim or stale projection supplies no effect permission.])

]
#behavior(title: "Stop acknowledgement is not terminal cancellation", area: "External job cleanup", level: "interface")[#given[An owned external job has a committed local stop cause.] #when[The service acknowledges a stop request.] #then[The request acceptance is retained.]#then[The job remains owned until authoritative terminal evidence settles it.]#then[No business route is resumed.]]
