#section(title: "Provider adapters and compiled composition", lead: "Substantial lifecycle behavior lives in core; application mappings remain recipes.", body: [
The #term("term-classification-wire") fixes receipt interpretation independently of fresh execution context.

#subsection(title: "Generation and classification")[
#answers(title: "LLM adapters", responsibility: [Bind independent llm_wire generation and classification capabilities to Fabric model or operation ports.], interface: [fabric/llm.model, graph/llm.decision and graph/classify.decision with typed input, fixed questions/wire and fresh request callback.], interactions: [Application supplies an http_gun.Client and reveal-closure credentials. Generation retains provider receipts and typed answer codec; classification retains labels, distributions, rubric, model, optional usage and evidence.], invariants: [One classification operation version fixes the pure wire and finite receipt bounds. Fresh live settings come only after policy admission and never enter durable data. Offline receipt decoding invokes neither network nor credential reveal.], failure: [Incompatible live byte limits above receipt bounds fail in typed preparation before credentials or I/O. Lower limits never prevent older receipt decoding. NotSent is Explain; possibly-sent or completed provider failures conservatively become Uncertain at graph operation boundary.])

]
#points([An endpoint override must implement the version's fixed protocol. Switching protocol requires another operation version, with compatible earlier deployed definitions retained.], [Confidence is optional concentration evidence; it is not probability that the chosen business answer is correct. Thresholds, route fallback and evaluation belong to the application.], [Inference, routing and admission are three decisions. A model can select admitted enum routes or bounded task lists; it cannot install code or bypass policy.])
#adr(6)
#subsection(title: "Workflow, MCP and identity recipes")[
#answers(title: "Consumer composition", responsibility: [Translate each package outcome explicitly while preserving its independent owner.], interface: [Retained compiled consumers for Saga tool, Relay typed tools/discovery/graph/serve/run-id, and Warden approvers. README and module-doc recipe copies are checked against consumer modules.], interactions: [Saga reports complete typed workflow outcome or operational error; consumer selects safe Explain/Uncertain projection and late settlement. Relay invocation renders native answer/evidence and run metadata. Warden verifies authentication without owning Fabric policy.], invariants: [Core depends on llm_wire, http_gun, json_blueprint and sinal; no Saga, Relay, Warden or Grind dependency. Adapters do not acquire universal retry/error/durability meanings.], failure: [MCP arbitrary schema/name admission is separate from listing. Remote read-only hints are application trust assertions, not proof a mutating effect is safe. Discovery preserves absent structured output separately from explicit null.])

]
#info(title: "Recipes remain executable examples")[The current Saga recipe is 59 formatted lines because typed reporting errors and full report projection carry real semantics; its check permits 60. Other recipe ceilings stay 50. Line count is a maintenance signal, not a reason to invent a shared public abstraction. The retired fabric_typesafe, fabric_saga and fabric_relay packages stay retired. #adr(3)]

])
#section(title: "Protocol-neutral invocation", lead: "Request ownership determines whether a bounded waiter cancels work.", body: [
#term("term-invocation") binds request lifetime to a reusable agent or graph service.

#subsection(title: "Service and idempotency")[
#answers(title: "Invocation service", responsibility: [Bind agent/graph execution once and return a portable response for any request transport.], interface: [invoke.agent, invoke.agent_with_history or invoke.graph creates Service; Request retains typed context/input, principal, optional key/correlation and disconnect selector. check validates a finite wait; default is 25 seconds.], interactions: [Key scopes include service name, runtime family and authenticated principal. Framed tuple hashing derives run id; same key/input reopens it. Changed correlation on retry does not change first accepted run correlation.], invariants: [Changed original input under the same key is key_reused, including changed imported history whose first message is unchanged. Agent services use fabric.matches_initial; graph services use graph.matches_initial. Shared services must set a stable authenticated principal; with_principal supplies identity scope and performs no authentication. Live context and cancellation selectors are never stored or compared as input.], failure: [Initial responses always retain attempted run id. Invalid wait, key reuse and incompatible input refuse the request. Agent StartUnconfirmed and agent/graph StoreUnavailable during admission return OutcomeUnknown. Unavailable keyed reopen or input verification also retains OutcomeUnknown. Other admission errors remain Refused. General read/await failures return Refused with code unavailable.])

]
#subsection(title: "Durable admission and outcome incorporation")[
#answers(title: "Application delivery composition", responsibility: [Bridge application acceptance and outcome incorporation without introducing another execution owner.], interface: [An existing transactional job or outbox retains an accepted application turn and its stable service, principal, key and original input. A worker invokes the existing service; the leased store and registered sweeper own run recovery.], interactions: [Acceptance and delivery publication commit together in the application's existing transaction. Fabric may begin later. After completion, an idempotent application transaction incorporates the retained answer and generated messages and records that the logical turn was applied.], invariants: [Retain the Fabric outcome until incorporation commits. The application checks its durable applied marker before delivery; an applied turn is never reinvoked after Fabric pruning. Shared pools or borrowed connections do not establish atomic Fabric admission with application writes.], failure: [Working remains in progress; approval/input suspension needs its declared continuation; uncertainty requires inspection or reconciliation of the same identity; ended failure and definite refusal remain separate. An absent answer alone establishes neither retry eligibility nor successful incorporation.])
#points([The application starts no second lease-renewal loop, abandoned-run scanner or competing queue for Fabric runs. Existing delivery retries cover the acceptance-to-start interval; Fabric recovery covers admitted runs.], [An application-authored per-turn graph can own result incorporation as an explicit operation after agent completion. Its application transaction must use a stable logical idempotency key; interruption after a possible commit requires reconciliation or truthful bounded replay.], [A graph moves incorporation into retained execution but does not make its initial admission atomic with application acceptance. The existing job or outbox still covers that interval. No adapter admit_in capability follows from sharing a database connection.])
#adr(13)

]
#subsection(title: "Wait and cancellation outcomes")[
#answers(title: "Request lifetime", responsibility: [Bound waiting while preserving the native run outcome and ownership obligations.], interface: [Response accessors expose answer, id, Kind, code, description and JSON facts; Kind distinguishes Answered, Working, AwaitingApproval, AwaitingInput, OutcomeUnknown, Unattended, Ended and Refused.], interactions: [Keyed work outlives the request and disconnect. Unkeyed in-flight work cancels on wait expiry or disconnect. Approval/reconciliation return immediately even for unkeyed work; application owns follow-up by id.], invariants: [Cancellation failure never claims stop. Completed answer that wins a cancellation race remains Answered. Cancelled/expired runs with unresolved local or child effects expose OutcomeUnknown.], failure: [Transport handler must keep invoke wait below its own request deadline. Unknown effects require status/reconciliation with original identity, not another effect submission. Unknown admission retains the attempted run id and existing error code. Retry the same principal/key or recover that run; an unknown response never authorizes a fresh logical submission.])

]
#behavior(title: "Unconfirmed admission preserves the attempted run", area: "Invocation ownership", level: "interface")[#given[Admission may have stored a run but its acknowledgement or keyed readback is unavailable.] #when[The invocation returns.] #then[The response classifies the outcome as unknown and retains the attempted run identity.] #then[A retry with the same principal and key names that same logical run.]]
#behavior(title: "Keyed retries retain the same logical run", area: "Invocation ownership", level: "interface")[#given[A stable service, principal and idempotency key already name a run.] #when[A request repeats the original input with a new correlation.] #then[The same run is opened.]#then[The first accepted correlation remains on its work.]]
#behavior(title: "Unkeyed wait expiry cancels in-flight work", area: "Invocation ownership", level: "interface")[#given[An unkeyed invocation still has live work.] #when[Its finite wait expires or the caller disconnects.] #then[Cancellation is requested for that run.]#then[The response preserves confirmed completion, unresolved effects or a cancellation failure truthfully.]]
