#section(title: "Durable store and runtime ownership", lead: "Revision CAS, leases and supervision answer separate questions.", visual: diagram(altitude: "L3", viewpoint: "runtime", title: "One runner owns isolated work and confirmed advancement", caption: [The runner requests a durable fence before a body. It commits the original result before publishing accepted facts. Backend callbacks and bodies are separately bounded; the observation path supplies no execution authority.], flow: "left-to-right", nodes: ((id: "runner", label: "Agent or graph runner", kind: "component", tint: "violet"), (id: "store", label: "Store port and registry", kind: "component", tint: "violet"), (id: "backend", label: "Configured backend", kind: "external-system"), (id: "body", label: "Application body", kind: "external-system"), (id: "sinal", label: "Sinal handler or forwarder", kind: "external-system")), edges: ((from: "runner", to: "store", relation: "call", label: "fence and result commits"), (from: "store", to: "backend", relation: "call", label: "bounded CAS callback"), (from: "store", to: "runner", relation: "dataflow", label: "confirmed revision or unknown"), (from: "runner", to: "body", relation: "call", label: "after fence; bounded task"), (from: "body", to: "runner", relation: "dataflow", label: "original invocation result"), (from: "runner", to: "sinal", relation: "pubsub", label: "accepted-state facts"))), body: [
A #term("term-lease") selects the execution driver. A #term("term-write-token") identifies the exact attempted write.

#subsection(title: "Record port and acknowledgement")[
#answers(title: "Backend port", responsibility: [Keep the latest encoded record and revision while allowing exactly one advancement of an expected revision.], interface: [Unleased get, insert and compare_and_set; leased current record/holder plus atomic Lease action. Errors are NotFound, AlreadyExists, Conflict, LeaseRefused or Unavailable.], interactions: [Insert stores revision 1; CAS stores expected+1 only if expected is current. Unavailable writes are checked by exact encoded bytes at exact target revision, including fresh write token.], invariants: [Two concurrent calls at one expected revision cannot both succeed across shared processes/machines. Encode once per logical write and reuse those bytes for confirmation; equivalent state from another writer is insufficient.], failure: [Backend callback crashes/timeouts become Unavailable. An unconfirmed insert becomes StartUnconfirmed and may arrive later. Reuse original id or cancel_stored rather than starting another logical run.])

]
#subsection(title: "Lease authority")[
#answers(title: "Leased store", responsibility: [Coordinate which node drives work without replacing the record revision authority.], interface: [LeasedBackend get/insert/CAS, now, renew, claim_expired and claim_ready. Holder is Free or Held(owner, live). Lease mutation is Hold, Claim, Seize or Release.], interactions: [Hold requires the named holder, including expired ownership; Claim permits free/same/expired owner; Seize and Release still require correct record revision. Renewal extends only live held leases and changes no execution revision.], invariants: [Running fences and work-in-flight commits require retained lease authority. A final commit releases with revision check. Store renews runners around lease/3 and stops local tasks on failed or lost renewal.], failure: [Live foreign lease is not recovered. Idle commands can apply without its runner when no work needs it. Foreign in-flight commands may return RunUnattended; cancellation can fence through storage. Claiming expired/ready work never grants routing without validation.])

]
#subsection(title: "Store supervision and draining")[
#answers(title: "Store lifecycle", responsibility: [Supervise and register agent/graph runners while isolating bounded backend callbacks.], interface: [store.in_memory, directory, new or leased; start/supervised, readiness, stop, with_drain and backend timeout. Store name/runtime owner is independent of the process that first starts a run.], interactions: [Without automatic recovery, the application supervises store.supervised. With automatic recovery, sweeper.supervised supplies the store subtree and ordered sweeper together; it replaces store.supervised. Admission starts after readiness. Stop closes acceptance and drains all owned runners including ones still delivering synchronous observations.], invariants: [Default drain is 25 seconds. Within the window a started effect can complete, its successor is saved but handed off without starting. Idle runs retain no runner. Bounded backend callbacks do not block unrelated store operations.], failure: [Forced task stop or unconfirmed handoff can remain uncertain. Drain summary separately records confirmed/failed/pending handoffs and forced/other exits; unavailable accounting is explicit. Stop result never erases durable evidence.])

]
#subsection(title: "Memory and directory boundaries")[

#points([In-memory records disappear when their owning store state disappears. They support deterministic testing and independent agent usefulness without database setup.], [Directory CAS uses host filesystem serialization and atomic record replacement. It can coordinate several VMs on one host, with no lease-driven multi-node ownership.], [Directory acknowledged writes survive process/VM loss within its documented filesystem assumptions, but directory entries are not fsynced. Power loss may lose a recent fence and permit re-execution; it is not production power-loss durability.], [Applications choose a database backend for production. The nested fabric_postgres layer owns PostgreSQL transactions, schema, indexes, migrations, projections and application-owned pool integration.])
#adr(5)

]
