#section(title: "Recovery discovery and retention", lead: "Scheduling and metadata guide recovery; saved execution state remains authority.", body: [
#term("term-discovery") supplies scheduling evidence. Only a complete #term("term-settled-family") qualifies for backend pruning checks.

#subsection(title: "Root registration and sweeper")[
#answers(title: "Sweeper", responsibility: [Find expired leases and changed/due idle work and recover through registered compatible roots.], interface: [sweeper.agent rebuilds live context. sweeper.graph rebuilds the complete graph and child runtimes against the supplied pinned store. Each builder has five seconds. sweeper.supervised supplies a RestForOne subtree containing the store followed by its sweeper; use it instead of store.supervised. Script-only start links to an already started store and caller.], interactions: [A boot scan precedes interval-based scans; the interval starts after each completed batch. A batch takes at most 50 expired leases and 50 changed idle dependencies without overlapping scans. Each candidate recovery has 30 seconds. Unknown identities are reported rather than executed. Mixed parent chains resolve exact root. Changed-child and due-wait projections share a bounded ready claim path.], invariants: [Notifications merely wake observation. Compatible definition, original attachment, lease, quota and policy checks still govern effects. Manual read/open/await never silently seize recovery ownership. Held work awaits lease expiry; a signal wait without a deadline needs explicit delivery.], failure: [Stale projections require refresh; missing children/roots, unreadable records and context-builder failure refuse recovery. Failed callbacks leave lease-expiry retry paths. The sweeper stops before the store drains, and restarts when the store restarts.])

]
#subsection(title: "Projection semantics")[
#answers(title: "Discovery, retention and statistics", responsibility: [Extract minimal versioned metadata for backend recovery, pruning and diagnostics without executing deployed callbacks.], interface: [store/discovery Wait(key, Changed/Poll/At); store/retention Metadata(run, parent, children, settled); store/statistics diagnostic projections; conformance checks backend extension guarantees.], interactions: [Discovery v13 tracks approval expiry and idle work; retention v12 includes agent/graph families and budget ledger. Backend refresh updates metadata while preserving execution bytes, revision, original ages and same-key observation times.], invariants: [Projection eligibility never authorizes an effect. Unknown/corrupt records do not qualify as finished, absent or safe to prune. An ended run with uncertain effects can remain unsettled.], failure: [Stale metadata can block recovery or pruning until repaired. Statistics are bounded operational diagnostics, not admission health or proof of no active external effect.])

]
#subsection(title: "Family-safe pruning")[

#points([A pruner must verify complete reciprocal family links, expected membership, all settled descendants, age and live-lease absence atomically. Retention.inspect alone grants no deletion authority.], [A missing acknowledged child, mismatched parent key, unknown format or unresolved owned job prevents pruning the complete family. Budget ledger links participate.], [A completed result and later compensation remain history. Deleting retained runs ends the idempotent reopening and replay-evidence window; applications own retention duration and external audit needs.], [PostgreSQL pruning, refresh/statistics and schema internals are specified by the nested adapter layer. Parent operations guidance owns startup, deployment, readiness and incident procedures.])
#adr(5)

]
#behavior(title: "Unknown metadata cannot authorize pruning", area: "Retention", level: "interface")[#given[A family contains an unreadable record, missing reciprocal member or unresolved effect.] #when[Retention is attempted.] #then[The family remains retained.]#then[An ended status is not treated as sufficient settlement evidence.]]

