#section(title: "End-to-end walkthrough", lead: "A source-based writing graph demonstrates typed control, human ownership and restart.", visual: sequence(title: "Committed decision before external publication", participants: ((id: "app", label: "Application", shape: "participant"), (id: "runtime", label: "Fabric", shape: "control"), (id: "store", label: "Store", shape: "database"), (id: "effect", label: "Publisher", shape: "boundary")), steps: (seq-msg("app", "runtime", "start with typed state"), seq-msg("runtime", "store", "confirm initial record"), seq-msg("runtime", "store", "retain review route and approval"), seq-msg("runtime", "app", "pending approval reference", dashed: true), seq-msg("app", "runtime", "proof and fresh context"), seq-msg("runtime", "store", "confirm exact body fence"), seq-msg("runtime", "effect", "publish with stable logical key"), seq-msg("effect", "runtime", "result or unresolved evidence", dashed: true), seq-msg("runtime", "store", "retain receipt and final state"), seq-msg("runtime", "app", "typed outcome and run id", dashed: true)), caption: [Network and credentials stay live. Every external effect follows its own permission and storage fence; observations do not control the sequence.]), body: [

#points([An application constructs one HTTP client, shared Approvers value, typed generation/classification operations, immutable review graph and supervised store. It completes backend migrations and projection refresh before sweeper startup and admission.], [A request chooses a RunId and correlation. The graph commits initial state before selecting source input, inspecting policy and fencing the generation body. Its native generation receipt and application state commit together.], [Review returns a typed choice and retained distribution. Application acceptance chooses publish, revise or rejection from declared destinations. A revision repeats a node with a new activation until the activation/work bounds stop it.], [Publication policy requests approval. No body runs while awaiting it. A request handler verifies a current credential for the exact requirement; approval rechecks policy with fresh application context. Expiry records rejection rather than assuming permission.], [A process loss after the publish fence leaves the publish effect uncertain unless its explicit idempotency contract resolves it. Recovery reuses earlier generation and review receipts and never reruns those decisions merely because context changed.], [The operator reconciles the original publication result. A cancelled or expired graph records the evidence with no success route. Retention can remove the complete family only after its external obligations settle and the application retention window ends.])

])
